  "description": "REAR EXTENSION, LOFT CONVERSION & OUTBUILDING",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p style=\"text-align: justify; \"><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Enlargement of a dwelling house (Class A)</span></u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> - The operations comprising the erection of a single storey rear extension, would consist of the enlargement of a dwelling house\r\nwithin the meaning of Class A of Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the Town &amp; Country\r\nPlanning (General Permitted Development)&nbsp;\r\n(England) Order 2015 \"the Order\" and would comply with the\r\ndevelopment tolerances set out in said Class A. The operation would therefore\r\nhave been granted planning permission by Article 3 of the Order.</span></span></p>",
    "<p style=\"text-align: justify; \"><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Enlargement of a dwelling house (Class B) </span></u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">- The operations comprising the erection of a hip to gable and rear dormer roof extensions, would consist of the enlargement of a dwelling house\r\nwithin the meaning of Class B of Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the Town &amp; Country\r\nPlanning (General Permitted Development)&nbsp;\r\n(England) Order 2015 \"the Order\" and would comply with the\r\ndevelopment tolerances set out in said Class B. The operation would therefore\r\nhave been granted planning permission by Article 3 of the Order.</span></span></p>",
    "<p style=\"text-align: justify; \"><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Alteration to the roof of the dwelling house (Class C)</span></u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> - The operations comprising the installation of x3 rooflights to the front roof slope, would consist of any other alteration to the roof of the\r\ndwelling house within the meaning of Class C of Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the\r\nTown &amp; Country Planning (General Permitted Development)&nbsp; (England) Order 2015 \"the Order\"\r\nand would comply with the development tolerances set out in said Class C. The\r\noperation would therefore have been granted planning permission by Article 3 of\r\nthe Order.</span></span></p>",
    "<p style=\"text-align: justify; \"><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Erection of an outbuilding (Class E) </span></u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">- The operations would consist of the erection of an outbuilding for uses\r\nincidental to that of the main house within the meaning of Class E of Part 1 of\r\nSchedule 2 to the Town & Country Planning (General Permitted Development)\r\n(England) Order 2015 \"the Order\" and would comply with the\r\ndevelopment tolerances set out in Class E. The operation would therefore have\r\nbeen granted planning permission by Article 3 of the Order.</span></span></p>"
  ],
